# GitHub issues → plan first

When the user points at a GitHub issue (URL, `#N`, or “issue N”):

1. Fetch it locally with `gh` (`gh issue view N`, optionally `--comments`).
2. Treat the work as **planning first**, not implementation — switch to / stay in **Plan Mode** (or propose the switch) before writing code.
3. Only implement after the plan is agreed (or the user explicitly says to skip planning / implement now).

Small, unambiguous fixes the user already scoped as “just do X” can skip planning; default for issues is plan first.
